  "description": "Roof extension to existing 2nd floor flat",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "By virtue of the scale, design, and massing of the large box dormer (which would exceed more than two thirds the average width of the original roof) would fail to retain a substantial element of the original rear roofslope and would constitute an overly-large roof extension that would fail to harmonise with the architectural composition of the original dwelling and create an alien feature from public viewpoints along the street scene. This dominance also gives rise to less than substantial harm to the Northwood Town Centre Conservation Area, which would not be outweighed by any public benefit. It is therefore considered that the proposal conflicts with Policies BE1 and HE1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part One Strategic Policies (2012), as well as DMHB1, DMHB11, DMHB12, and DMHD1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020)."
  ],
